1
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,800
"Blue Lips"

2
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:13,800
(Episode 9)

3
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:46,079
Teng Mo, where are you?

4
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:47,715
Why aren't you answering your phone?

5
00:01:47,739 --> 00:01:48,859
Did something happen to you?

6
00:02:58,039 --> 00:02:59,159
Brother Mo gave this to you.

7
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:01,760
Where is he?

8
00:03:03,659 --> 00:03:04,659
I don't know.

9
00:03:08,079 --> 00:03:09,079
He said

10
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:11,280
to live your life well.

11
00:03:34,059 --> 00:03:35,179
That one is Jupiter.

12
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:36,559
West of the moon.

13
00:03:37,219 --> 00:03:39,000
And to the north is Sirius.

14
00:03:40,199 --> 00:03:41,839
So as long as the distance is far enough,

15
00:03:43,059 --> 00:03:44,299
no matter how big something is,

16
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,159
it will seem tiny.

17
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,420
It's the same with people's troubles.

18
00:03:54,539 --> 00:03:55,539
Shixian.

19
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:57,940
Your nights

20
00:03:58,679 --> 00:04:00,539
should be saved for beautiful things.

21
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:07,360
Is it beautiful?

22
00:04:07,719 --> 00:04:08,719
It is.

23
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:55,500
You...

24
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:56,940
Get up right now!

25
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,659
You brat!

26
00:04:59,139 --> 00:05:00,780
Get up! Get up!

27
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,120
You've been home for a month,

28
00:05:02,199 --> 00:05:03,359
and all you do is lie around!

29
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:04,499
The sun is already high in the sky,

30
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,260
and you're still sleeping!

31
00:05:05,261 --> 00:05:06,598
You're in your thirties,

32
00:05:06,599 --> 00:05:08,319
and you still don't have your act together.

33
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:09,739
Why did I even raise you?

34
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:10,380
Get up!
Get up right now!

35
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:11,440
Mom.

36
00:05:11,719 --> 00:05:12,719
Get up!

37
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:15,678
The bedroom of an older,
single, unmarried man

38
00:05:15,679 --> 00:05:17,460
is off-limits to the opposite sex.

39
00:05:18,119 --> 00:05:19,980
So you know you're older and unmarried!

40
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,939
When Auntie Lee tried to set you up,

41
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:23,400
you didn't even go meet the girl.

42
00:05:23,599 --> 00:05:25,159
And you have the nerve to say that now?

43
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:27,500
She wouldn't be interested in me anyway.

44
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:30,138
You don't even have a proper job.

45
00:05:30,139 --> 00:05:31,539
Why would she be interested in you?

46
00:05:32,079 --> 00:05:32,639
Perfect.

47
00:05:32,980 --> 00:05:34,300
I'm not interested in her either.

48
00:05:35,219 --> 00:05:36,479
Look at you, acting like this.

49
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,980
And you're still being picky!

50
00:05:38,139 --> 00:05:39,739
Look at what a mess this room is.

51
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,320
Clothes piled up everywhere.

52
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:42,980
You don't even shave.

53
00:05:43,739 --> 00:05:44,739
And this pillowcase,

54
00:05:45,079 --> 00:05:46,639
are you using it as a sharpening cloth?

55
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:50,860
Who talks about their
precious son like that?

56
00:05:52,579 --> 00:05:54,559
What precious son?

57
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:57,260
Who has a precious son in his thirties?

58
00:05:57,780 --> 00:05:59,039
In his thirties?

59
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:00,598
Watch your words, okay?

60
00:06:00,599 --> 00:06:01,679
I'm only thirty.

61
00:06:04,199 --> 00:06:05,199
Cut the crap.

62
00:06:05,260 --> 00:06:07,178
Hurry up and clean your room,

63
00:06:07,179 --> 00:06:08,819
then help your dad change the fish water.

64
00:06:09,059 --> 00:06:10,059
Fine.

65
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:11,320
Ms. Hu,

66
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,800
do I get paid?

67
00:06:14,099 --> 00:06:15,099
I'll smack you!

68
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,360
Paid?

69
00:06:16,519 --> 00:06:17,519
Get out of bed right now!

70
00:06:18,940 --> 00:06:20,180
Honestly, day in and day out...

71
00:06:29,739 --> 00:06:30,739
Teng Mo.

72
00:06:31,679 --> 00:06:32,679
Teng Mo!

73
00:06:33,239 --> 00:06:34,799
You can't drain that much water.

74
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:36,440
The fish will die if you drain that much.

75
00:06:36,539 --> 00:06:38,159
Go get the water I use for the fish.

76
00:06:44,739 --> 00:06:45,739
This kid...

77
00:06:55,119 --> 00:06:56,839
Are you counting grains of rice over there?

78
00:06:57,380 --> 00:06:59,038
If you're done eating, clean it up.

79
00:06:59,039 --> 00:07:00,760
If you're not done, hurry up and eat.

80
00:07:06,059 --> 00:07:07,299
Eat some more dishes.

81
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:08,500
Don't just eat plain rice.

82
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,638
What's wrong with you?

83
00:07:16,639 --> 00:07:17,880
Is something on your mind?

84
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:19,760
You look like you've lost your soul.

85
00:07:21,539 --> 00:07:22,539
No.

86
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:23,920
You say no,

87
00:07:24,579 --> 00:07:26,519
but he almost killed the fish I'm raising!

88
00:07:27,079 --> 00:07:28,518
We can barely take care of the people here,

89
00:07:28,519 --> 00:07:30,316
and you're still worrying
about your stupid fish?

90
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:31,480
What stupid fish?

91
00:07:31,599 --> 00:07:33,159
Those are purebred tropical fish.

92
00:07:33,539 --> 00:07:34,659
They're very precious, okay?

93
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:36,558
They die and get thrown out every day.

94
00:07:36,559 --> 00:07:37,239
Of course they're precious.

95
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:39,520
One of these days, I should
just throw you out too.

96
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:40,880
Enough.

97
00:07:41,119 --> 00:07:42,119
Look how old you are,

98
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:43,360
and you're still bickering.

99
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,480
And you.

100
00:07:45,699 --> 00:07:46,679
Auntie Lee said

101
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:48,058
she wants to set you up again.

102
00:07:48,059 --> 00:07:49,460
You have to go meet her this time.

103
00:07:51,039 --> 00:07:51,699
This Auntie Lee...

104
00:07:51,719 --> 00:07:53,300
Her retirement life is really rich.

105
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:56,000
She spends every day ruining
the lives of single youths.

106
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:57,739
And she ruins them two at a time.

107
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:04,420
Just saying.

108
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:07,880
I've actually met the girl this time.

109
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:09,219
She's fair and pretty,

110
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:10,239
and has a good job.

111
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:11,579
A doctor at the hospital.

112
00:08:12,639 --> 00:08:13,738
She's well-educated and reasonable.

113
00:08:13,739 --> 00:08:15,059
She looks very well-brought-up.

114
00:08:15,719 --> 00:08:16,719
Her age is suitable too.

115
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,240
Exactly two years younger than you.

116
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,840
With such great qualifications,

117
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:24,736
I can save yourself the trip.
She won't be interested in me.

118
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:25,760
You...

119
00:08:27,020 --> 00:08:29,720
She just wants to find
someone family-oriented.

120
00:08:30,060 --> 00:08:30,920
As for age

121
00:08:31,079 --> 00:08:31,960
and other things,

122
00:08:31,961 --> 00:08:33,761
as long as it's passable,
she's fine with it.

123
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:36,219
The main thing is she's too busy with work,

124
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:38,340
so she needs someone who
can take care of the family.

125
00:08:38,579 --> 00:08:39,959
Anyway, you don't have a job right now,

126
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,520
and you're just idling at home all day.

127
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:43,500
Even so,

128
00:08:43,899 --> 00:08:45,658
it's only because
Auntie Lee and I are close

129
00:08:45,659 --> 00:08:47,760
that she saved you
the priority to meet her.

130
00:08:51,319 --> 00:08:53,039
There's even an internal referral for this?

131
00:08:54,119 --> 00:08:55,978
Your dad and I are over a
hundred years old combined.

132
00:08:55,979 --> 00:08:57,696
How many more years are
you going to drag this out?

133
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:00,460
Okay, okay, I'll go.

134
00:09:01,699 --> 00:09:02,920
I'll go, alright?

135
00:09:06,439 --> 00:09:07,759
Make sure you freshen
up when the time comes.

136
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:08,760
Shave your beard.

137
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:09,960
Don't look so sloppy.

138
00:09:15,819 --> 00:09:17,140
You really make me worry.

139
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:18,520
Day in and day out.

140
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:28,399
Auntie Lee mentioned

141
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:29,639
that Mr. Teng previously

142
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:31,359
did business over in Jinyang.

143
00:09:33,819 --> 00:09:34,819
Yes.

144
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:36,420
Do you mind if I ask

145
00:09:36,619 --> 00:09:37,779
what kind of business it was?

146
00:09:40,279 --> 00:09:41,279
I ran a shop.

147
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:43,180
An adult novelty store.

148
00:09:46,279 --> 00:09:47,760
That must have been quite profitable.

149
00:09:50,279 --> 00:09:51,279
It was alright.

150
00:09:52,239 --> 00:09:54,159
Are you planning to move
back to Fengzhou now?

151
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:00,159
That's the plan for now.

152
00:10:00,939 --> 00:10:01,979
I also want to see

153
00:10:02,399 --> 00:10:03,800
if I can find a job.

154
00:10:06,039 --> 00:10:07,239
Mr. Teng,

155
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:09,460
do you have someone in your heart?

156
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:16,880
It seems you do.

157
00:10:17,579 --> 00:10:18,199
You know,

158
00:10:18,399 --> 00:10:20,719
this is the first time you've
looked at me while speaking.

159
00:10:21,739 --> 00:10:22,739
I'm sorry.

160
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:23,800
That was rude of me.

161
00:10:26,619 --> 00:10:28,579
It seems we're in a similar situation.

162
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:30,738
Then let's treat this afternoon tea

163
00:10:30,739 --> 00:10:33,359
as two fellow sufferers
of forced matchmaking

164
00:10:33,479 --> 00:10:34,859
taking a rare moment to relax.

165
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:41,260
What is the person in
Mr. Teng's heart like?

166
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,399
A very pure person,

167
00:10:50,979 --> 00:10:53,439
and someone who easily gets hurt.

168
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:59,020
You came back to Fengzhou because of them as well?

169
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:04,679
Since you like them so much,

170
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:05,800
why did you leave?

171
00:11:06,399 --> 00:11:07,399
We broke up.

172
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:12,539
They're getting married.

173
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:15,420
Leaving them

174
00:11:15,739 --> 00:11:17,500
is my way of giving them my blessing.

175
00:11:19,833 --> 00:11:21,133
Did they say that themselves?

176
00:11:24,119 --> 00:11:25,119
But,

177
00:11:25,279 --> 00:11:26,899
even if they did say it himself,

178
00:11:26,979 --> 00:11:28,099
it wouldn't change anything.

179
00:11:28,659 --> 00:11:30,800
There's a pretty big age gap between us.

180
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,159
Being with them

181
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:37,420
would only stop them from
pursuing their own happiness.

182
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:39,739
Besides,

183
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:43,800
we never actually told each
other we liked one another.

184
00:11:45,399 --> 00:11:47,460
We just share some
happy memories, that's all.

185
00:11:49,439 --> 00:11:50,180
But isn't love

186
00:11:50,181 --> 00:11:52,140
built on memories?

187
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:00,140
But looking at you,

188
00:12:01,159 --> 00:12:02,539
it's like looking in a mirror.

189
00:12:04,079 --> 00:12:05,079
To think the two of us

190
00:12:05,239 --> 00:12:07,539
are avoiding our true feelings,

191
00:12:08,180 --> 00:12:10,079
and instead are sitting in this cafe

192
00:12:10,819 --> 00:12:11,939
feeling sorry for ourselves.

193
00:12:12,779 --> 00:12:14,119
It's truly absurd.

194
00:12:17,859 --> 00:12:19,939
Although the information
you've given me is limited,

195
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:21,140
my intuition tells me

196
00:12:21,359 --> 00:12:22,479
that between the two of you,

197
00:12:22,939 --> 00:12:24,340
there must be a misunderstanding.

198
00:12:26,420 --> 00:12:27,420
You're right.

199
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:28,760
To be exact,

200
00:12:29,340 --> 00:12:31,659
it all started because
of a misunderstanding.

201
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:34,978
So, have all these misunderstandings

202
00:12:34,979 --> 00:12:36,100
been cleared up now?

203
00:12:38,199 --> 00:12:39,199
It doesn't matter.

204
00:12:39,939 --> 00:12:41,060
From the very beginning,

205
00:12:42,199 --> 00:12:43,880
it was all just the shadow of his lover.

206
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:49,560
Sis.

207
00:12:57,199 --> 00:12:57,539
Sis.

208
00:12:58,060 --> 00:12:59,715
The specialists from Jing City are
coming for a consultation today.

209
00:12:59,739 --> 00:13:00,739
We still have a chance.

210
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,000
This Dr. Jiang

211
00:13:02,039 --> 00:13:02,880
is the most authoritative expert

212
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:04,520
in this entire field in our country.

213
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:05,960
He'll definitely have a way.

214
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:09,420
Really?

215
00:13:10,359 --> 00:13:11,359
Really.

216
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:13,500
We're definitely going to get better.

217
00:13:21,579 --> 00:13:22,739
So you're saying

218
00:13:23,079 --> 00:13:25,340
those pills were likely
used to treat an illness?

219
00:13:25,619 --> 00:13:27,619
I'm just saying it's a possibility.

220
00:13:29,579 --> 00:13:30,759
For some patients

221
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:32,659
with pulmonary arterial
hypertension, Vandacon

222
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:34,140
is a life-saving drug.

223
00:13:35,119 --> 00:13:37,840
These patients experience increased
pulmonary vascular resistance,

224
00:13:38,039 --> 00:13:39,039
leading to hypoxia.

225
00:13:39,399 --> 00:13:41,420
Their lips turn blue and purple over time.

226
00:13:42,199 --> 00:13:42,800
That's why

227
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:45,039
it's also known as the blue lip disease.

228
00:13:46,539 --> 00:13:48,259
You said the first time you saw him,

229
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:49,579
he had blue lips.

230
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,000
So,

231
00:13:51,239 --> 00:13:52,539
I'm just relying on my intuition

232
00:13:52,939 --> 00:13:53,760
to make a bold assumption.

233
00:13:53,859 --> 00:13:56,180
Maybe there's a connection here.

234
00:13:57,479 --> 00:13:59,880
Could he have bought them for that girl?

235
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:02,239
Can this disease be cured?

236
00:14:03,819 --> 00:14:06,419
Very few people in the country
know about this disease right now,

237
00:14:06,579 --> 00:14:08,699
so it's easily misdiagnosed or missed.

238
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:11,720
By the time many patients are diagnosed,

239
00:14:11,859 --> 00:14:13,539
it's already in the middle to late stages.

240
00:14:13,659 --> 00:14:15,600
For many patients, after the onset,

241
00:14:16,079 --> 00:14:17,478
the disease progresses rapidly,

242
00:14:17,479 --> 00:14:18,880
often catching them off guard.

243
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:26,759
The patient has already missed
the best window for treatment

244
00:14:26,760 --> 00:14:28,156
and can only rely on a
heart-lung transplant.

245
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:29,180
But

246
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:31,180
her current indicators
aren't very optimistic.

247
00:14:31,399 --> 00:14:32,680
Even if we find a match,

248
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:35,295
she might not be able to
undergo the transplant surgery.

249
00:14:35,319 --> 00:14:36,639
You need to be mentally prepared.

250
00:14:45,199 --> 00:14:47,720
Is the mortality rate for
this disease very high?

251
00:14:49,220 --> 00:14:51,000
According to current research data,

252
00:14:51,539 --> 00:14:54,180
the five-year survival rate
might be around twenty percent.

253
00:14:55,859 --> 00:14:56,960
But there are exceptions.

254
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,479
With long-term medication control,

255
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:01,960
it's possible to prolong life.

256
00:15:02,439 --> 00:15:05,539
However, the targeted drugs
that can treat this disease right now

257
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:07,479
are all imported Bosentan.

258
00:15:07,939 --> 00:15:09,100
The price is incredibly high.

259
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:10,660
Many patients can't afford it,

260
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:13,759
so they can only use the cheaper Vandacon

261
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:14,760
as a substitute

262
00:15:14,939 --> 00:15:15,939
to barely hang on.

263
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:19,199
I think

264
00:15:19,619 --> 00:15:21,479
maybe he's in the same situation.

265
00:15:23,819 --> 00:15:24,819
No wonder

266
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:27,520
he kept telling me

267
00:15:28,199 --> 00:15:29,380
it wasn't what I thought.

268
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:31,500
I was so foolish.

269
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,640
I only knew to tell him not to take them.

270
00:15:36,539 --> 00:15:37,539
Mr. Teng,

271
00:15:37,779 --> 00:15:39,419
it seems that when you left,

272
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:40,820
you left behind a lot of mysteries.

273
00:15:43,140 --> 00:15:44,140
I-

274
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:47,960
If my assumption is true,

275
00:15:48,439 --> 00:15:50,359
right now, whether it's for him

276
00:15:50,539 --> 00:15:51,720
or the people around him,

277
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:52,960
the situation

278
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:54,380
is very difficult.

279
00:16:04,159 --> 00:16:05,159
Sis.

280
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:08,920
Sis.

281
00:16:09,180 --> 00:16:10,180
I think

282
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:12,340
we should go to the city
and get it checked again.

283
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:15,239
Doctors make mistakes sometimes too, right?

284
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:17,960
Listen to me, Shixian.

285
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:21,699
We need to think about
what to do in the future.

286
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:26,499
With my physical condition,

287
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:29,220
going all the way to Jing
City is completely unrealistic.

288
00:16:30,779 --> 00:16:32,899
Secondly, I don't want
you to drain our savings

289
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:34,419
and sell the house

290
00:16:34,420 --> 00:16:36,260
to gamble on an impossible outcome.

291
00:16:40,140 --> 00:16:41,960
You still have a long future ahead of you.

292
00:16:43,779 --> 00:16:46,420
I don't want to see you
end up with nothing.

293
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:51,020
Sis,

294
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:53,180
I'm going to get mad if
you keep talking like this.

295
00:16:54,939 --> 00:16:57,560
So you're not even
listening to your sister now?

296
00:16:59,500 --> 00:16:59,939
Sis!

297
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:01,420
Are you okay?

298
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,520
I'm sorry, Sis.

299
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:05,020
I-

300
00:17:05,340 --> 00:17:06,579
I shouldn't have made you mad.

301
00:17:09,180 --> 00:17:10,180
Don't cry, Shixian.

302
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:13,039
Shixian, don't cry.

303
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:16,020
It's really no big deal.

304
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:19,899
It's just that everyone

305
00:17:21,760 --> 00:17:23,420
has a different ending.

306
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:27,859
Hello?

307
00:17:28,359 --> 00:17:29,359
Ah Heng.

308
00:17:29,659 --> 00:17:31,339
Do you know where Wu Shixian is right now?

309
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:36,640
Got it.

310
00:17:41,079 --> 00:17:42,079
Okay.

311
00:17:44,319 --> 00:17:45,619
What are you packing for?

312
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:46,760
Are you heading out again?

313
00:17:47,399 --> 00:17:47,720
Dad,

314
00:17:48,079 --> 00:17:49,438
something came up in Jinyang.

315
00:17:49,439 --> 00:17:50,439
I need to head back.

316
00:17:53,079 --> 00:17:53,899
Is it serious?

317
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:55,239
Do you want us to go with you?

318
00:17:55,579 --> 00:17:56,899
It's fine, I can go by myself.

319
00:17:57,340 --> 00:17:58,340
As for Mom,

320
00:17:58,380 --> 00:17:59,380
I'll explain it to her.

321
00:18:01,439 --> 00:18:02,039
Alright then.

322
00:18:02,340 --> 00:18:03,459
Take good care of yourself.

323
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:04,460
Stay safe.

324
00:18:07,279 --> 00:18:08,279
Dad,

325
00:18:08,939 --> 00:18:09,939
I'm sorry.

326
00:18:10,039 --> 00:18:11,039
Coming back this time,

327
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:12,740
I didn't get to spend much time with you.

328
00:18:14,399 --> 00:18:16,119
We can take care of ourselves.

329
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:17,380
Just look out for yourself.

330
00:18:42,699 --> 00:18:43,699
Shixian,

331
00:18:45,079 --> 00:18:46,859
what about that girlfriend you were seeing?

332
00:18:48,619 --> 00:18:49,899
Did you guys break up?

333
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:53,060
I don't have a girlfriend.

334
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:56,399
We were never even together.

335
00:18:59,819 --> 00:19:01,239
Is it because of me

336
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:03,159
that she couldn't accept you?

337
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:05,640
No.

338
00:19:06,039 --> 00:19:07,460
We're just regular friends.

339
00:19:08,819 --> 00:19:10,340
I just got the wrong idea.

340
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:12,380
Besides,

341
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:15,700
she doesn't even know about my situation.

342
00:19:16,199 --> 00:19:17,199
Don't worry about it.

343
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Sis,

344
00:19:22,119 --> 00:19:24,520
I can handle my
own matters myself.

345
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:26,240
You don't need to worry about me.

346
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:30,039
I just feel that

347
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:32,520
a kid your age

348
00:19:33,220 --> 00:19:34,439
should be going to class,

349
00:19:34,699 --> 00:19:35,699
studying,

350
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:36,760
and dating.

351
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:38,140
But instead, because of-

352
00:19:38,279 --> 00:19:39,279
Sis,

353
00:19:39,779 --> 00:19:41,159
stop saying things like that.

354
00:19:43,319 --> 00:19:45,659
Isn't it only right that we
take care of each other?

355
00:19:50,119 --> 00:19:52,260
My little brother is so mature.

356
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,140
He's handsome,

357
00:19:54,619 --> 00:19:55,680
does well in school,

358
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:57,319
and has a kind heart.

359
00:19:57,960 --> 00:19:59,899
If she can't see all these great qualities,

360
00:20:00,260 --> 00:20:01,420
she's the one with bad taste.

361
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:03,500
If it's over, it's over.

362
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:04,760
I'm not sad.

363
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:15,100
Brother Hao,

364
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:16,860
could you possibly lend me a bit more?

365
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:19,960
Bro,

366
00:20:20,819 --> 00:20:22,099
even if I took you apart

367
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:23,079
piece by piece,

368
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:25,260
you'd be worth a hundred grand at most.

369
00:20:25,899 --> 00:20:27,299
How am I supposed to lend you more?

370
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:31,020
Brother Hao,

371
00:20:31,399 --> 00:20:32,699
it's a real emergency.

372
00:20:34,180 --> 00:20:35,399
Please help me out.

373
00:20:36,380 --> 00:20:37,380
I'm truly

374
00:20:37,899 --> 00:20:39,039
out of options.

375
00:20:39,579 --> 00:20:40,579
I'm begging you.

376
00:20:40,979 --> 00:20:41,979
Watch out!

377
00:20:44,159 --> 00:20:45,159
Curly!

378
00:20:46,239 --> 00:20:47,239
Curly!

379
00:20:47,479 --> 00:20:48,060
Are you okay?
I'm fine, bro.

380
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:50,039
Call a doctor!

381
00:20:51,479 --> 00:20:51,979
Hu-zi,

382
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:53,380
get a doctor here!

383
00:20:54,239 --> 00:20:55,399
Hang in there, hang in there.

384
00:20:56,060 --> 00:20:56,560
It's okay.

385
00:20:56,899 --> 00:20:57,899
It's okay.
